WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:09.676
♪♪

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.677
Good morning, my dear.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.678
♪♪

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:12.679
Action!

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:17.476
♪♪

00:00:17.476 --> 00:00:22.856
So Tehran is an espionage
thriller about a young Mossad
agent

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:24.733
Niv:
sent to Tehran for a special
mission. 

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:25.859
♪♪

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:29.071
Niv:
It's the first time that you see
on screen a completely different

00:00:29.071 --> 00:00:31.615
Niv:
humane angle of the
Iranian / Israeli conflict.

00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:34.993
It shows the messy grey area of
life.

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:37.829
♪♪

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:39.373
Glenn Close:
There's no black and white.

00:00:39.373 --> 00:00:40.457
♪♪

00:00:40.457 --> 00:00:41.667
And I think that's truthful.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.460
♪♪

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.795
From the first season,

00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:46.255
Dana Eden:
Tamar Rabinyan...

00:00:47.464 --> 00:00:48.924
Dana Eden:
...infiltrates Tehran.

00:00:49.216 --> 00:00:50.884
The mission basically failed.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:51.802
♪♪

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.264
In the second season, we are two
months later.

00:00:55.806 --> 00:00:57.766
Niv:
Tamar and Milad, they're stuck.

00:00:57.766 --> 00:00:59.726
Niv:
Hiding from the Mossad and the
Sepah.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:02.729
Faraz has been chasing her for a
long time.

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:05.565
Sherbin:
They are seemingly determined to
get out of Iran...

00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:08.986
...but you know, in this show,
plans don't work out.

00:01:08.986 --> 00:01:10.404
♪♪

00:01:10.404 --> 00:01:11.405
I can't leave yet.

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:15.534
Her war against the regime
becomes really, really personal.

00:01:16.118 --> 00:01:19.329
I know how to get to Assid
Mohammadi and I want to take him
out.

00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:20.622
How?

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:21.790
Tamar:
His son, Peiyman.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.834
♪♪

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:28.005
Season two deals a lot with the
hypocrisy and double standard.

00:01:28.005 --> 00:01:29.298
♪♪

00:01:29.298 --> 00:01:34.386
In Tehran you have very wealthy
people connected to the regime.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.848
Dana Eden:
Tamar is in a more
dangerous position.

00:01:37.889 --> 00:01:39.975
Niv Sultan:
She needs to get deep
undercover.

00:01:39.975 --> 00:01:41.727
Niv Sultan:
Near the most important people
in Tehran

00:01:41.727 --> 00:01:43.103
Niv Sultan:
and the most dangerous people.

00:01:43.312 --> 00:01:44.479
She has a lot to lose.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:47.232
Glenn Close:
Each person has their own story.

00:01:47.858 --> 00:01:50.861
You're not always sure exactly
who's antagonist and who's
protagonist.

00:01:50.902 --> 00:01:54.489
Daniel Sirkin:
Faraz is the most feared man in
the Iranian Intelligence.

00:01:54.531 --> 00:01:56.616
Because of his work,

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.076
Shila Ommi:
his wife was kidnapped.

00:01:58.076 --> 00:01:59.369
Shaun Toub:
And he was shot.

00:02:00.037 --> 00:02:02.831
So Naahid is dealing with PTSD.

00:02:02.831 --> 00:02:04.708
♪♪

00:02:04.708 --> 00:02:07.002
Shaun Toub:
And Faraz is a different man
now.

00:02:07.002 --> 00:02:08.003
Sort of a has-been.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.424
He wants to be back where he
was.

00:02:12.424 --> 00:02:14.593
♪♪

00:02:14.593 --> 00:02:16.887
Glenn Close is joining us this
season.

00:02:18.472 --> 00:02:21.141
She's what you would expect from
Glenn Close and much more.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:24.144
Glenn Close:
Marjan is a very high profile
psychiatrist

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:25.937
and deep cover Mossad agent.

00:02:25.937 --> 00:02:26.813
♪♪

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:29.399
Glenn Close:
I come as a therapist for
Naahid,

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:30.442
Glenn Close;
to get to Faraz.

00:02:30.776 --> 00:02:32.819
Glenn Close:
That's one of those very
conflicted moments

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:35.822
Glenn Close:
as a psychiatrist verse a Mossad
agent.

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:41.995
In our series we offer a new
perspective on Tehran.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:47.542
Dana Eden:
We really wanted to see the
people in Iran, how do they live, what do they think.

00:02:47.542 --> 00:02:50.212
You really feel like you're deep
in another culture.

00:02:50.212 --> 00:02:51.421
♪♪

00:02:51.421 --> 00:02:53.715
Niv Sultan:
It's not only about the
action.

00:02:53.715 --> 00:02:54.925
There's so many layers.

00:02:54.925 --> 00:02:55.842
We can trust him?

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.427
Yes, but can he handle it?

00:02:57.427 --> 00:02:59.805
It's high stakes, but there's a
lot of emotion in it.

00:02:59.805 --> 00:03:01.264
This season is much more

00:03:01.264 --> 00:03:04.518
exciting, dangerous,
heartbreaking.

00:03:04.518 --> 00:03:07.437
Glenn Close:
It's really tense and fast
moving,

00:03:07.437 --> 00:03:09.106
and just great entertainment.

00:03:09.106 --> 00:03:09.773
♪♪

00:03:09.773 --> 00:03:10.982
It's so much fun.

00:03:10.982 --> 00:03:12.442
♪♪

00:03:12.442 --> 00:03:14.528
(Explosion)

00:03:14.528 --> 00:03:16.613
♪♪

